\section{Inputs}{

The block takes any number of inputs, including none.
\itemize{
\item The first link into the block is \code{data}. A script written for one input
reads \code{data}, as it would in a function.
\item Every link also reads by its own name: the link name, or \code{.arg1},
\code{.arg2}, ... for a link that has none. Only the links without a name are
counted, so next to one named link the first unnamed one is \code{.arg1}.
Links are named where they are drawn: "Edit link" or "Edit inputs" in
the dock.
\item The block is variadic (\verb{function(id, ...args)}), so the order of the
links decides which one is \code{data}. A link that is removed and drawn
again comes last, and \code{data} is then another input. A script with more
than one input should read each by its own name, which does not move.
A link named \code{data} is always \code{data}.
\item With no input connected, \code{data} is \code{NULL} and the script is a source: it
reads a file, calls an API or builds a data frame itself.
}

On export each input name is replaced by the id of the upstream block, so
the exported code reads like a script someone wrote by hand.
